# Sources for the disputed election and Front cohort: Fakhreddin Azimi,
# Iran: The Crisis of Democracy, 1941–1953, pp. 207–208; Ervand Abrahamian,
# Iran Between Two Revolutions, ch. 5, pp. 250–267.
# The recurring committee work and its effects are counterfactual.
title: Electoral Committee
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: parliamentary_affairs
view-if: electoral_committee_timer <= 0 and majles_convened = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; electoral_committee_timer = 5
card-image: img/majlis_1940s.jpg

= Electoral Committee

Before the Sixteenth {!<span class="term term-parliament">!}Majles{!</span>!}
convenes, [? if front_formed = 0: cooperating candidates and opposition circles ?][? if front_formed = 1: the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} ?]
must distinguish rumor from a
usable election record. Constituency reports can reveal patterns, legal
petitions can force precise claims, and a public register can connect local
complaints without pretending that every return is already known.

Choose where the committee will put its limited effort this month.

[? if election_project = "Candidate coordination": Earlier candidate meetings
have left the committee a set of negotiated constituencies and contacts. ?]
[? if election_project = "Election observation": Earlier observers have left
the committee comparable reports of voting and interference. ?]
[? if election_project = "Funded opposition campaign": Earlier campaign work
has left selected candidates with printing, contacts, and local organization. ?]
[? if election_project = "Constituency report archive": The committee already
has a common collection of constituency reports. ?]
[? if election_project = "Constituency test cases": Lawyers have already
prepared selected constituency complaints for formal argument. ?]
[? if election_project = "Public election register": A provisional public
register already gives editors and candidates a common point of reference. ?]
[? if election_project_stage > 0: The committee is therefore revising an
existing record rather than beginning with a blank map. ?]

- @electoral_reports
- @electoral_case
- @electoral_register
- @return_card

@electoral_reports
title: Collect return and interference reports
subtitle: A common archive lets scattered complaints be compared before they become accusations
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_project = "Constituency report archive";
Q.election_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.election_project_stage > 2;
Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.organizational_reach += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.independent_nationalists_organization += mature ? 1 : 2;
Q.support_provincial += mature ? 0 : 2;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable) {
        place.scenario.legal_defense += mature ? 1 : 4;
    }
}
!}

The committee distributes a common reporting form and asks local contacts to
separate what they observed from what they heard. Incomplete reports remain
marked as such rather than being promoted into a national result.

[? if front_formed = 0: The cooperating circles gain ?][? if front_formed = 1: The {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} gains ?] a
wider and more disciplined picture of the election.
Converting those reports into a constitutional case still requires another
step.
[? if election_project_stage > 2: The archive now grows by correction and
corroboration more than by discovery. Repeating the collection preserves its
value, but cannot supply local contacts the opposition never had. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@electoral_case
title: Prepare constitutional petitions
subtitle: One resource lets <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Iran Party</span> lawyers turn selected complaints into arguments the chamber must answer
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource for filings and counsel.
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_project = "Constituency test cases";
Q.election_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.election_project_stage > 2;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.constitutional_legitimacy += mature ? 1 : 4;
Q.parliamentary_procedure_legitimacy += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.iran_party_relation += mature ? 0 : 2;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable) {
        place.scenario.legal_defense += mature ? 1 : 3;
        place.scenario.credential_contest = "prepared";
    }
}
!}

Lawyers and party organizers turn the strongest documented complaints into
petitions with named constituencies, dates, and requested remedies.
{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}
figures value a method that can be defended inside constitutional institutions.

The case becomes more precise and procedurally credible. Reports that cannot
meet that standard remain outside the filing.
[? if election_project_stage > 2: The strongest test cases have already been
identified. Further legal spending improves their presentation, but cannot
turn the weaker complaints into equally persuasive cases. ?]

- @post_event: Continue

@electoral_register
title: Publish a provisional constituency register
subtitle: One resource prints a provisional register that invites scrutiny—and exposes every blank the opposition cannot yet fill
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 resource for printing and distribution.
on-arrival: {!
Q.election_project = "Public election register";
Q.election_project_stage += 1;
var mature = Q.election_project_stage > 2;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.press_capacity += mature ? 1 : 4;
Q.public_mandate += mature ? 1 : 3;
Q.shah_relation -= 1;
Q.support_professional += mature ? 0 : 2;
Q.support_bazaar += mature ? 0 : 2;
for (var place of Q.majles_places) {
    if (place.scenario.contestable) {
        place.scenario.campaign_investment += mature ? 1 : 3;
    }
}
!}

The committee publishes only returns and objections it can identify by place,
labeling missing or disputed evidence instead of filling it with estimates.
Friendly papers can now compare claims against one common register.

Public scrutiny grows, as does the
{!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court's{!</span>!} irritation with the
opposition's challenge. The document is explicitly provisional and must be revised as
better evidence arrives.
[? if election_project_stage > 2: A revised edition corrects and consolidates
the public record, but attracts less new attention than the first publication
while renewing the {!<span class="term term-royalist">!}Court's{!</span>!}
resentment. ?]

- @post_event: Continue
